      "reason": "Qa4 quietly aligns the Queen behind Ba3 and also attacks Bd4. In the strongest reviewed Bb2 defence, Bc5+ reveals the Queen check on the a-file while the Bishop attacks Qa7; Kb1 allows Bxa7. This introduces quiet Queen setup followed by Bishop double threat, rather than repeating the existing Queen-and-Knight back-rank capture. Moving the attacked White Queen instead exposes the Bishop on d4; stronger replies were compared in the saved engine probes.",
      "goal": "material",
